# showrunner runtime state — not source
# Campaign-scoped state. Every file below this line is also listed flat, from before campaigns
# had their own directories; the list was never widened when the layout moved, so a checkout
# carrying a campaign reported as permanently dirty and `--version` answered "dirty — this sha
# overstates what is here" on a clean tree. A warning that is always on is one nobody reads.
campaigns/
sessions.json
graph.db
graph.db-*
locks/
scratch/
campaign.json
routing.jsonl
baseline.json
integration-commit.json
config.local.json
campaign.json.lock
events.jsonl
hook-heartbeat.jsonl
fail-open.jsonl
waiting.jsonl
*.lock
seen-issues.json
# Which sessions the wake gate has already told. Runtime, per-machine, and pruned on
# write -- a ledger of who has been spoken to is not source, and committing it would
# silence the gate for every clone that inherited somebody else's session ids.
wake-gate-seen.json
